# Model outputs. Every one of these is reproducible from a workbook plus a
# scenario config, so the repository carries the inputs and the code, not the
# results. `results/` alone reached 82 MB on five scenarios.
results/

# Snakemake's own bookkeeping: DAG metadata, per-run logs, conda/singularity
# caches, and the incomplete-output markers it writes mid-run.
.snakemake/

# Audit and verification working directories, regenerable by re-running the
# workflow against a scenario.
.audit/

# The archive of superseded material. Deliberately kept on disk but out of the
# repository: it is, by definition, the pile of things that are not needed, and
# it holds the 456 KB source notebook plus old run logs and audit HTML.
older_files/

# The test suite. Kept on disk and runnable locally with `python -m pytest
# tests -q`, but not published: 3,000 lines of regression tests is not what a
# reader of this repository is looking for. Nothing in the workflow or CI
# imports it, so excluding it breaks nothing.
tests/

# Internal migration and verification records. These three link only to each
# other -- nothing in the README, the guide or tools/build_docs.py references
# them -- so removing them together leaves no dangling link. They index
# artefacts under .audit/ that are not published either, and they describe how
# this project was migrated rather than how to use it.
docs/audit.md
docs/MIGRATION_STATUS.md
docs/PARITY_AUDIT.md

# Built documentation. `tools/build_docs.py` regenerates it from docs/.
_site/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# Excel lock files and the backups `template.force` leaves behind. A lock file
# starting with ~$ appears while a workbook is open and must never be committed:
# `workbook_path` already skips it, but it would still confuse a reader.
~$*.xlsx
*.xlsx.bak
*.bak

# Solver logs written into the working directory
gurobi.log
*.ilp
*.lp

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
